IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa22-part30.l4: Part 30 of the Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), ss 994 to 999 (lines 13934-13993 of
-- ukpga-2006-46.txt): protection of members against unfair prejudice. LAYER 1: the law, objectively.
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; it is not the
-- official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text". Quote lines are copied from it by a
-- script and checked by srcrefs.py.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer; see NOTES.md).
--   JUST TRUE   the text says the case is within the rule.
--   JUST FALSE  the text says no in its own words (a "means" definition, an "if" / "where" / "unless" condition
--               that fails, a flat negative). Each such branch carries  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "<words>"
--   NOTHING     the text does not decide (silent, list not closed, includes, undefined term, points outside the
--               text, limited by its own wording). Each such branch carries  -- NOTHING-kind (<why>)
--   A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- A fact a witness can state is a BOOLEAN input. A judgment the text hands to someone else (the court is satisfied,
-- it appears to the Secretary of State) is a BOOLEAN input too, never guessed. An answer another part gives is a
-- MAYBE BOOLEAN input named for the section that answers it (a seam, PLAN.md section 4).
-- Pounds are never in the Act for a level on the standard scale: that is an input of the seat layer.
-- Days are counted by adding them to the date of the event; the day of the event is not counted. NOTES.md, fork F1.

§ `Part 30 -- Protection of members against unfair prejudice`

§§ `Main provisions`

-- ---- s 994: Petition by company member --------------------------------------------------------------------

-- (1A) Removal of the company's auditor, for the purposes of subsection (1)(a), is treated as unfairly
-- prejudicial to the interests of some part of the members if it is on either of two grounds.
-- src:13940 | (1A) For the purposes of subsection (1)(a), a removal of the company's auditor from office—
-- src:13941 | (a) on grounds of divergence of opinions on accounting treatments or audit procedures, or
-- src:13942 | (b) on any other improper grounds,
-- src:13943 | shall be treated as being unfairly prejudicial to the interests of some part of the company's members.
@ref s 994(1A) Petition by company member (src:13940-13943)
GIVEN `the company's auditor has been removed from office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the removal was on grounds of divergence of opinions on accounting treatments or audit procedures` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the removal was on any other improper grounds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 994(1A) the removal of the company's auditor is treated as unfairly prejudicial to some part of the members` MEANS
    IF     `the company's auditor has been removed from office`
       AND (   `the removal was on grounds of divergence of opinions on accounting treatments or audit procedures`
            OR `the removal was on any other improper grounds`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a removal of the company's auditor from office— (a) on grounds of divergence of opinions ... or (b) on any other improper grounds, shall be treated as being unfairly prejudicial"; the text deems nothing about a removal on other grounds or no removal

-- (2) A non-member to whom shares have been transferred or transmitted by operation of law is treated as a member.
-- src:13944 | (2) The provisions of this Part apply to a person who is not a member of a company but to whom shares in the company have been transferred or transmitted by operation of law as they apply to a member of a company.
@ref s 994(2) Petition by company member (src:13944)
GIVEN `shares in the company have been transferred or transmitted to the person by operation of law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 994(2) the person who is not a member is treated as a member for the purposes of Part 30` MEANS
    IF `shares in the company have been transferred or transmitted to the person by operation of law`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a person who is not a member of a company but to whom shares in the company have been transferred or transmitted by operation of law"; other non-members are not mentioned

-- (3) "company" in section 994 (and so far as applicable in the rest of Part 30) means a company within the meaning
-- of this Act. Paragraph (b) is shown as blank in this text.
-- src:13945 | (3) In this section, and so far as applicable for the purposes of this section in the other provisions of this Part, “company” means—
-- src:13946 | (a) a company within the meaning of this Act, or
-- src:13947 | (b) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
@ref s 994(3) Petition by company member (src:13945-13947)
GIVEN `s 1(1) the body is a company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 994(3) the body is a company for the purposes of section 994` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 1(1) the body is a company`
    WHEN JUST isCompany THEN
        IF isCompany
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“company” means— (a) a company within the meaning of this Act"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the answer is s 1(1), which the keel gives, and "unless the context otherwise requires" may leave it open

-- (1)(a) The first ground: the company's affairs are being or have been conducted in a manner unfairly prejudicial.
-- src:13938 | (a) that the company's affairs are being or have been conducted in a manner that is unfairly prejudicial to the interests of members generally or of some part of its members (including at least himself), or
@ref s 994(1)(a) Petition by company member (src:13938)
GIVEN `the company's affairs are being or have been conducted in a manner that is unfairly prejudicial to the interests of members generally` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company's affairs are being or have been conducted in a manner that is unfairly prejudicial to the interests of some part of its members` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that part of the members includes at least the person petitioning` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 994(1A) the removal of the company's auditor is treated as unfairly prejudicial to some part of the members` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 994(1)(a) the ground of conduct of the company's affairs is made out` MEANS
    IF     `the company's affairs are being or have been conducted in a manner that is unfairly prejudicial to the interests of members generally`
       OR (    (   `the company's affairs are being or have been conducted in a manner that is unfairly prejudicial to the interests of some part of its members`
                OR (`s 994(1A) the removal of the company's auditor is treated as unfairly prejudicial to some part of the members` EQUALS JUST TRUE))
           AND `that part of the members includes at least the person petitioning`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on the ground—"; the text lists the grounds without saying that a case outside them cannot be petitioned on

-- (1)(b) The second ground: an actual or proposed act or omission of the company is or would be so prejudicial.
-- src:13939 | (b) that an actual or proposed act or omission of the company (including an act or omission on its behalf) is or would be so prejudicial.
@ref s 994(1)(b) Petition by company member (src:13939)
GIVEN `an actual or proposed act or omission of the company (including an act or omission on its behalf) is or would be unfairly prejudicial to the interests of members generally or of some part of its members` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 994(1)(b) the ground of an actual or proposed act or omission of the company is made out` MEANS
    IF `an actual or proposed act or omission of the company (including an act or omission on its behalf) is or would be unfairly prejudicial to the interests of members generally or of some part of its members`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on the ground—"; the text lists the grounds without saying that a case outside them cannot be petitioned on

-- (1) A member may apply to the court by petition for an order under Part 30 on either ground. A person treated as a
-- member by subsection (2) has the same standing. The member status itself is section 112's (a seam).
-- src:13936 | 994 Petition by company member
-- src:13937 | (1) A member of a company may apply to the court by petition for an order under this Part on the ground—
-- src:13938 | (a) that the company's affairs are being or have been conducted in a manner that is unfairly prejudicial to the interests of members generally or of some part of its members (including at least himself), or
-- src:13939 | (b) that an actual or proposed act or omission of the company (including an act or omission on its behalf) is or would be so prejudicial.
@ref s 994(1) Petition by company member (src:13936-13939)
GIVEN `s 112 the person is a member of the company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 994(2) the person who is not a member is treated as a member for the purposes of Part 30` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 994(3) the body is a company for the purposes of section 994` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 994(1)(a) the ground of conduct of the company's affairs is made out` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 994(1)(b) the ground of an actual or proposed act or omission of the company is made out` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 994(1) the person may apply to the court by petition for an order under Part 30` MEANS
    IF `s 994(3) the body is a company for the purposes of section 994` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“company” means ... a company within the meaning of this Act"
    ELSE IF     (   `s 112 the person is a member of the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
                 OR `s 994(2) the person who is not a member is treated as a member for the purposes of Part 30` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
            AND (   `s 994(1)(a) the ground of conduct of the company's affairs is made out` EQUALS JUST TRUE
                 OR `s 994(1)(b) the ground of an actual or proposed act or omission of the company is made out` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
            AND `s 994(3) the body is a company for the purposes of section 994` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A member of a company may apply to the court by petition ... on the ground—"; the text does not say that a non-member, or a member without these grounds, may not

-- ---- s 995: Petition by Secretary of State ------------------------------------------------------------------

-- (1) The section applies to a company in respect of which one of four things has happened. Whether it happened is a
-- fact the person can state; the officials and the instruments they used are in the text's own words.
-- src:13949 | (1) This section applies to a company in respect of which—
-- src:13950 | (a) the Secretary of State has received a report under section 437 of the Companies Act 1985 (c. 6) (inspector's report);
-- src:13951 | (b) the Secretary of State has exercised his powers under section 447 or 448 of that Act (powers to require documents and information or to enter and search premises);
-- src:13952 | (c) the Secretary of State , the Financial Conduct Authority, the Prudential Regulation Authority or the Bank of England has exercised his or its powers under Part 11 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (c. 8) (information gathering and investigations); or
-- src:13953 | (d) the Secretary of State has received a report from an investigator appointed by him , the Financial Conduct Authority, the Prudential Regulation Authority or the Bank of England under that Part.
@ref s 995(1) Petition by Secretary of State (src:13949-13953)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State has received a report under section 437 of the Companies Act 1985 (inspector's report)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State has exercised his powers under section 447 or 448 of the Companies Act 1985 (powers to require documents and information or to enter and search premises)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State, the Financial Conduct Authority, the Prudential Regulation Authority or the Bank of England has exercised powers under Part 11 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (information gathering and investigations)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State has received a report from an investigator appointed by him, the Financial Conduct Authority, the Prudential Regulation Authority or the Bank of England under Part 11 of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 995(1) section 995 applies to the company` MEANS
    IF     `the Secretary of State has received a report under section 437 of the Companies Act 1985 (inspector's report)`
       OR  `the Secretary of State has exercised his powers under section 447 or 448 of the Companies Act 1985 (powers to require documents and information or to enter and search premises)`
       OR  `the Secretary of State, the Financial Conduct Authority, the Prudential Regulation Authority or the Bank of England has exercised powers under Part 11 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (information gathering and investigations)`
       OR  `the Secretary of State has received a report from an investigator appointed by him, the Financial Conduct Authority, the Prudential Regulation Authority or the Bank of England under Part 11 of that Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies to a company in respect of which—"; no "only" closes the list of four

-- (4) "company" in section 995 means any body corporate liable to be wound up under the Insolvency Act 1986 or the
-- Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989. Whether a body is liable to be wound up is the borrowed fact.
-- src:13959 | (4) In this section, and so far as applicable for the purposes of this section in the other provisions of this Part, “company” means any body corporate that is liable to be wound up under the Insolvency Act 1986 (c. 45) or the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989 (S.I. 1989/2405 (N.I. 19)).
@ref s 995(4) Petition by Secretary of State (src:13959)
GIVEN `the person is a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body corporate is liable to be wound up under the Insolvency Act 1986 or the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 995(4) the body is a company for the purposes of section 995` MEANS
    IF `the person is a body corporate` AND `the body corporate is liable to be wound up under the Insolvency Act 1986 or the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“company” means any body corporate that is liable to be wound up under the Insolvency Act 1986 ... or the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989"

-- (2) If it appears to the Secretary of State that, in the case of such a company, the affairs are being or have been
-- conducted unfairly prejudicially or an act or omission is or would be so, he may apply to the court by petition.
-- "It appears to the Secretary of State" is the Secretary of State's judgment: an input, never guessed.
-- src:13954 | (2) If it appears to the Secretary of State that in the case of such a company—
-- src:13955 | (a) the company's affairs are being or have been conducted in a manner that is unfairly prejudicial to the interests of members generally or of some part of its members, or
-- src:13956 | (b) an actual or proposed act or omission of the company (including an act or omission on its behalf) is or would be so prejudicial,
-- src:13957 | he may apply to the court by petition for an order under this Part.
@ref s 995(2) Petition by Secretary of State (src:13954-13957)
GIVEN `s 995(1) section 995 applies to the company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 995(4) the body is a company for the purposes of section 995` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the Secretary of State that the company's affairs are being or have been conducted in a manner that is unfairly prejudicial to the interests of members generally or of some part of its members` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the Secretary of State that an actual or proposed act or omission of the company (including an act or omission on its behalf) is or would be so prejudicial` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 995(2) the Secretary of State may apply to the court by petition for an order under Part 30` MEANS
    IF `s 995(4) the body is a company for the purposes of section 995` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“company” means any body corporate that is liable to be wound up"
    ELSE IF `s 995(1) section 995 applies to the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `s 995(4) the body is a company for the purposes of section 995` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN IF     `it appears to the Secretary of State that the company's affairs are being or have been conducted in a manner that is unfairly prejudicial to the interests of members generally or of some part of its members`
                 OR  `it appears to the Secretary of State that an actual or proposed act or omission of the company (including an act or omission on its behalf) is or would be so prejudicial`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If it appears to the Secretary of State that ... he may apply to the court by petition"; neither judgment appears to him, and the text does not say that he may not (name-test sweep of 2026-11-12, fork F16: the other reading is JUST FALSE, a failed "if" read as the text's own no)
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies to a company in respect of which"; or the seam is open

-- (3) The Secretary of State may petition under Part 30 in addition to, or instead of, presenting a winding-up petition.
-- src:13958 | (3) The Secretary of State may do this in addition to, or instead of, presenting a petition for the winding up of the company.
@ref s 995(3) Petition by Secretary of State (src:13958)
GIVEN `s 995(2) the Secretary of State may apply to the court by petition for an order under Part 30` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State has presented a petition for the winding up of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 995(3) the Secretary of State may petition under Part 30 whether or not he has presented a winding-up petition` MEANS
    -- Both limbs, "in addition to" (a winding-up petition has been presented) and "instead of" (it has not), give the same answer.
    IF `the Secretary of State has presented a petition for the winding up of the company`
    THEN `s 995(2) the Secretary of State may apply to the court by petition for an order under Part 30`
    ELSE `s 995(2) the Secretary of State may apply to the court by petition for an order under Part 30`

-- ---- s 996: Powers of the court under this Part ------------------------------------------------------------

-- (1) If the court is satisfied that a petition under this Part is well founded, it may make such order as it thinks
-- fit for giving relief in respect of the matters complained of. "Satisfied" is the court's judgment: an input.
-- src:13961 | (1) If the court is satisfied that a petition under this Part is well founded, it may make such order as it thinks fit for giving relief in respect of the matters complained of.
@ref s 996(1) Powers of the court under this Part (src:13961)
GIVEN `the court is satisfied that the petition under Part 30 is well founded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 996(1) the court may make such order as it thinks fit for giving relief in respect of the matters complained of` MEANS
    IF `the court is satisfied that the petition under Part 30 is well founded`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the court is satisfied that a petition under this Part is well founded, it may make such order"; the court is not so satisfied, and the text does not say that it may not (name-test sweep of 2026-11-12, fork F17: the other reading is JUST FALSE, a failed "if" read as the text's own no)

-- (2) Without prejudice to the generality of subsection (1), the order may contain any of five kinds of provision.
-- src:13962 | (2) Without prejudice to the generality of subsection (1), the court's order may—
-- src:13963 | (a) regulate the conduct of the company's affairs in the future;
-- src:13964 | (b) require the company—
-- src:13965 | (i) to refrain from doing or continuing an act complained of, or
-- src:13966 | (ii) to do an act that the petitioner has complained it has omitted to do;
-- src:13967 | (c) authorise civil proceedings to be brought in the name and on behalf of the company by such person or persons and on such terms as the court may direct;
-- src:13968 | (d) require the company not to make any, or any specified, alterations in its articles without the leave of the court;
-- src:13969 | (e) provide for the purchase of the shares of any members of the company by other members or by the company itself and, in the case of a purchase by the company itself, the reduction of the company's capital accordingly.
@ref s 996(2) Powers of the court under this Part (src:13962-13969)
DECLARE `s 996(2) kind of provision` IS ONE OF
    `s 996(2)(a) regulate the conduct of the company's affairs in the future`
    `s 996(2)(b)(i) require the company to refrain from doing or continuing an act complained of`
    `s 996(2)(b)(ii) require the company to do an act that the petitioner has complained it has omitted to do`
    `s 996(2)(c) authorise civil proceedings to be brought in the name and on behalf of the company`
    `s 996(2)(d) require the company not to make any, or any specified, alterations in its articles without the leave of the court`
    `s 996(2)(e) provide for the purchase of the shares of any members of the company by other members or by the company itself`
    `s 996(2) any other provision for giving relief under subsection (1)`

@ref s 996(2) Powers of the court under this Part (src:13962-13969)
GIVEN `s 996(1) the court may make such order as it thinks fit for giving relief in respect of the matters complained of` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      provision IS A `s 996(2) kind of provision`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 996(2) the court's order may contain the provision` MEANS
    -- The five listed kinds, and any other, are all within subsection (1): subsection (2) is "without prejudice to the generality" of it.
    CONSIDER `s 996(1) the court may make such order as it thinks fit for giving relief in respect of the matters complained of`
    WHEN JUST mayOrder THEN
        IF mayOrder
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the court is satisfied that a petition under this Part is well founded, it may make such order as it thinks fit" (subsection (2) is without prejudice to subsection (1) and rests on its gate; the court is not so satisfied, and the text does not say that its order may not contain the provision) (name-test sweep of 2026-11-12, fork F18: the other reading is JUST FALSE, a failed "if" read as the text's own no)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the court's satisfaction is the court's judgment and is not known

-- (2)(e) In the case of a purchase by the company itself, the order provides for the reduction of the company's
-- capital accordingly.
-- src:13969 | (e) provide for the purchase of the shares of any members of the company by other members or by the company itself and, in the case of a purchase by the company itself, the reduction of the company's capital accordingly.
@ref s 996(2)(e) Powers of the court under this Part (src:13969)
GIVEN `the order provides for the purchase of shares by the company itself` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 996(2)(e) the order provides for the reduction of the company's capital accordingly` MEANS
    IF `the order provides for the purchase of shares by the company itself`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the case of a purchase by the company itself, the reduction of the company's capital accordingly"; a purchase by other members carries no statement about capital

§§ `Supplementary provisions`

-- ---- s 997: Application of general rule-making powers -------------------------------------------------------
-- Machinery: the power to make rules under section 411 of the Insolvency Act 1986 applies to petitions under this Part.
-- Inert, reason 2 (rule-making powers). No L4 rule; see NOTES.md.
-- src:13972 | The power to make rules under section 411 of the Insolvency Act 1986 (c. 45) or Article 359 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989 (S.I. 1989/2405 (N.I. 19)), so far as relating to a winding-up petition, applies for the purposes of a petition under this Part.
§§ `s 997 Application of general rule-making powers (inert: machinery)`

-- ---- s 998: Copy of order affecting company's constitution to be delivered to registrar ----------------------

-- days after a date: the date N days after the date of an event, the day of the event not counted (fork F1).
GIVEN `the date of the event` IS A DATE
      `the number of days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s 998(2) the date a number of days after the date of an event` MEANS
    Date (DATE_DAY `the date of the event` PLUS `the number of days`) (DATE_MONTH `the date of the event`) (DATE_YEAR `the date of the event`)

-- (1) Where an order under Part 30 alters the company's constitution, or gives leave to alter it, the company must
-- deliver a copy of the order to the registrar.
-- src:13974 | (1) Where an order of the court under this Part—
-- src:13975 | (a) alters the company's constitution, or
-- src:13976 | (b) gives leave for the company to make any, or any specified, alterations to its constitution,
-- src:13977 | the company must deliver a copy of the order to the registrar.
@ref s 998(1) Copy of order affecting company's constitution to be delivered to registrar (src:13974-13977)
GIVEN `the order of the court under Part 30 alters the company's constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order of the court under Part 30 gives leave for the company to make any, or any specified, alterations to its constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 998(1) the company must deliver a copy of the order to the registrar` MEANS
    IF     `the order of the court under Part 30 alters the company's constitution`
       OR  `the order of the court under Part 30 gives leave for the company to make any, or any specified, alterations to its constitution`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an order of the court under this Part— (a) alters the company's constitution, or (b) gives leave ... the company must deliver a copy of the order to the registrar"

-- (2) It must do so within 14 days from the making of the order or such longer period as the court may allow.
-- The longer period, if the court allowed one, is a number of days from the making of the order; a period that is
-- not longer than 14 days adds nothing.
-- src:13978 | (2) It must do so within 14 days from the making of the order or such longer period as the court may allow.
@ref s 998(2) Copy of order affecting company's constitution to be delivered to registrar (src:13978)
GIVEN `the longer period the court allowed, in days from the making of the order, if any` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 998(2) the number of days allowed for delivering the copy of the order to the registrar` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the longer period the court allowed, in days from the making of the order, if any`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 14
    WHEN JUST allowed THEN
        IF allowed GREATER THAN 14
        THEN allowed
        ELSE 14

@ref s 998(2) Copy of order affecting company's constitution to be delivered to registrar (src:13978)
GIVEN `the date the order was made` IS A DATE
      `the longer period the court allowed, in days from the making of the order, if any` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s 998(2) the last day for delivering the copy of the order to the registrar` MEANS
    `s 998(2) the date a number of days after the date of an event` `the date the order was made` (`s 998(2) the number of days allowed for delivering the copy of the order to the registrar` `the longer period the court allowed, in days from the making of the order, if any`)

@ref s 998(2) Copy of order affecting company's constitution to be delivered to registrar (src:13978)
GIVEN `the date the order was made` IS A DATE
      `the longer period the court allowed, in days from the making of the order, if any` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the date the copy of the order was delivered to the registrar` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 998(2) the copy of the order was delivered to the registrar within the time allowed` MEANS
    IF `the date the copy of the order was delivered to the registrar` AT MOST `s 998(2) the last day for delivering the copy of the order to the registrar` `the date the order was made` `the longer period the court allowed, in days from the making of the order, if any`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 14 days from the making of the order or such longer period as the court may allow"

-- (1)-(2) as a regulative rule: the company MUST deliver a copy of the order to the registrar WITHIN the days allowed
-- (days are this file's clock), and BREACHes if it does not. Run with #TRACE in coa22-tests-part30.l4. The same
-- duty is also encoded above as decision functions, because the stable binary cannot assert on a trace.
DECLARE `s 998 act of the company` IS ONE OF
    `s 998 deliver a copy of the order to the registrar`

-- src:13974 | (1) Where an order of the court under this Part—
-- src:13975 | (a) alters the company's constitution, or
-- src:13976 | (b) gives leave for the company to make any, or any specified, alterations to its constitution,
-- src:13977 | the company must deliver a copy of the order to the registrar.
-- src:13978 | (2) It must do so within 14 days from the making of the order or such longer period as the court may allow.
@ref s 998(1) Copy of order affecting company's constitution to be delivered to registrar (src:13974-13978)
GIVEN `the order of the court under Part 30 alters the company's constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order of the court under Part 30 gives leave for the company to make any, or any specified, alterations to its constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the longer period the court allowed, in days from the making of the order, if any` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 998 act of the company`
`s 998(1)-(2) the company's duty to deliver a copy of the order to the registrar` MEANS
    IF `s 998(1) the company must deliver a copy of the order to the registrar` `the order of the court under Part 30 alters the company's constitution` `the order of the court under Part 30 gives leave for the company to make any, or any specified, alterations to its constitution` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY Company
         MUST `s 998 deliver a copy of the order to the registrar`
         WITHIN `s 998(2) the number of days allowed for delivering the copy of the order to the registrar` `the longer period the court allowed, in days from the making of the order, if any`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "the copy of the order was not delivered to the registrar within 14 days from the making of the order or such longer period as the court allowed"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- The company makes default in complying with section 998 if the duty applies (subsection (1)) and the last day
-- (subsection (2)) has passed without a copy of the order having been delivered by then. A derived rule, not a
-- provision: section 998(3) speaks of "default in complying with this section" without defining it (fork F2).
-- src:13974 | (1) Where an order of the court under this Part—
-- src:13975 | (a) alters the company's constitution, or
-- src:13976 | (b) gives leave for the company to make any, or any specified, alterations to its constitution,
-- src:13977 | the company must deliver a copy of the order to the registrar.
-- src:13978 | (2) It must do so within 14 days from the making of the order or such longer period as the court may allow.
@ref s 998(3) Copy of order affecting company's constitution to be delivered to registrar (src:13974-13978)
GIVEN `the order of the court under Part 30 alters the company's constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order of the court under Part 30 gives leave for the company to make any, or any specified, alterations to its constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the order was made` IS A DATE
      `the longer period the court allowed, in days from the making of the order, if any` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the date the copy of the order was delivered to the registrar, if it has been` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 998(3) the company has made default in complying with section 998` MEANS
    IF `s 998(1) the company must deliver a copy of the order to the registrar` `the order of the court under Part 30 alters the company's constitution` `the order of the court under Part 30 gives leave for the company to make any, or any specified, alterations to its constitution` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an order of the court under this Part— (a) alters the company's constitution, or (b) gives leave"
    ELSE IF `the date asked about` AT MOST `s 998(2) the last day for delivering the copy of the order to the registrar` `the date the order was made` `the longer period the court allowed, in days from the making of the order, if any`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 14 days from the making of the order or such longer period as the court may allow" (the time has not run out)
         ELSE CONSIDER `the date the copy of the order was delivered to the registrar, if it has been`
              WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN JUST delivered THEN
                  IF delivered AT MOST `s 998(2) the last day for delivering the copy of the order to the registrar` `the date the order was made` `the longer period the court allowed, in days from the making of the order, if any`
                  THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 14 days from the making of the order or such longer period as the court may allow" (delivered in time)
                  ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (3) If a company makes default in complying with section 998, an offence is committed by the company and by every
-- officer of the company who is in default.
-- src:13979 | (3) If a company makes default in complying with this section, an offence is committed by—
-- src:13980 | (a) the company, and
-- src:13981 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 998(3) Copy of order affecting company's constitution to be delivered to registrar (src:13979-13981)
GIVEN `the company makes default in complying with section 998` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 998(3)(a) the company commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `the company makes default in complying with section 998`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company makes default in complying with this section, an offence is committed by"

@ref s 998(3) Copy of order affecting company's constitution to be delivered to registrar (src:13979-13981)
GIVEN `the company makes default in complying with section 998` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 998(3)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the company makes default in complying with section 998`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company makes default in complying with this section, an offence is committed by"
    ELSE IF `the person is an officer of the company` AND `s 1121 the officer is in default` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every officer of the company who is in default"; a person who is not an officer, or whom section 1121 does not find in default, is not named, and the seam may be open


-- (4) A person guilty of an offence under section 998 is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3
-- on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3.
-- Penalty OF  how convicted, imprisonment, fine, daily default fine, imprisonment and fine together
-- src:13982 | (4) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 998(4) Copy of order affecting company's constitution to be delivered to registrar (src:13982)
`s 998(4) the penalty for a person guilty of an offence under section 998` MEANS
    Penalty OF `on summary conviction`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1), JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1), FALSE

-- A conversion, not a provision: the Act names a level on the standard scale and the statutory maximum, and the pounds they
-- stand for are set outside the Act (inputs, never guessed). This turns a `Fine limit` into pounds for any part's penalty.
-- src:13982 | (4) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 998(4) Copy of order affecting company's constitution to be delivered to registrar (src:13982)
GIVEN limit IS A MAYBE `Fine limit`
      `the amount in pounds that the level on the standard scale named in the fine limit stands for` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount in pounds of the statutory maximum` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 998(4) the amount in pounds of the fine limit` MEANS
    CONSIDER limit
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the penalty states no fine
    WHEN JUST fineLimit THEN
        CONSIDER fineLimit
        WHEN `a fine without a stated limit` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "a fine" with no stated limit has no amount in pounds
        WHEN `a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` fraction THEN JUST (`the amount in pounds of the statutory maximum` TIMES fraction)
        WHEN `a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` level fraction THEN JUST (`the amount in pounds that the level on the standard scale named in the fine limit stands for` TIMES fraction)
        WHEN `a fine not exceeding an amount in pounds` pounds THEN JUST pounds

-- ---- s 999: Supplementary provisions where company's constitution altered ---------------------------------

-- (1) The section applies where an order under Part 30 alters a company's constitution.
-- src:13984 | (1) This section applies where an order under this Part alters a company's constitution.
@ref s 999(1) Supplementary provisions where company's constitution altered (src:13984)
GIVEN `the order of the court under Part 30 alters the company's constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 999(1) section 999 applies` MEANS
    IF `the order of the court under Part 30 alters the company's constitution`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies where an order under this Part alters a company's constitution"; no "only" closes the scope

-- (2)(a) If the order amends the company's articles, the copy delivered under section 998 must be accompanied by a
-- copy of the articles as amended.
-- src:13985 | (2) If the order amends—
-- src:13986 | (a) a company's articles, or
@ref s 999(2)(a) Supplementary provisions where company's constitution altered (src:13985-13986)
GIVEN `s 999(1) section 999 applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the order amends the company's articles` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 999(2)(a) the copy of the order delivered to the registrar must be accompanied by a copy of the company's articles as amended` MEANS
    IF `s 999(1) section 999 applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN IF `the order amends the company's articles`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the order amends— (a) a company's articles ... the copy of the order ... must be accompanied by a copy of the company's articles"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies where an order under this Part alters a company's constitution"

-- (2)(b) If the order amends a resolution or agreement to which Chapter 3 of Part 3 applies, the copy must be
-- accompanied by a copy of that resolution or agreement as amended. Chapter 3 of Part 3 is a seam (section 29).
-- src:13985 | (2) If the order amends—
-- src:13986 | (a) a company's articles, or
-- src:13987 | (b) any resolution or agreement to which Chapter 3 of Part 3 applies (resolution or agreement affecting a company's constitution),
-- src:13988 | the copy of the order delivered to the registrar by the company under section 998 must be accompanied by a copy of the company's articles, or the resolution or agreement in question, as amended.
@ref s 999(2)(b) Supplementary provisions where company's constitution altered (src:13985-13988)
GIVEN `s 999(1) section 999 applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the order amends a resolution or agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 29 the resolution or agreement is one to which Chapter 3 of Part 3 applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 999(2)(b) the copy of the order delivered to the registrar must be accompanied by a copy of the resolution or agreement as amended` MEANS
    IF `s 999(1) section 999 applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN IF NOT (`the order amends a resolution or agreement`)
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the order amends— ... (b) any resolution or agreement to which Chapter 3 of Part 3 applies"
         ELSE CONSIDER `s 29 the resolution or agreement is one to which Chapter 3 of Part 3 applies`
              WHEN JUST chapter3 THEN
                  IF chapter3
                  THEN JUST TRUE
                  ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any resolution or agreement to which Chapter 3 of Part 3 applies"
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether Chapter 3 of Part 3 applies is section 29's answer
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies where an order under this Part alters a company's constitution"

-- (3) Every copy of the company's articles issued by the company after the order is made must be accompanied by a copy
-- of the order, unless the effect of the order has been incorporated into the articles by amendment.
-- src:13989 | (3) Every copy of a company's articles issued by the company after the order is made must be accompanied by a copy of the order, unless the effect of the order has been incorporated into the articles by amendment.
@ref s 999(3) Supplementary provisions where company's constitution altered (src:13989)
GIVEN `s 999(1) section 999 applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the copy of the articles is issued by the company after the order is made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the effect of the order has been incorporated into the articles by amendment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 999(3) the copy of the articles issued by the company must be accompanied by a copy of the order` MEANS
    IF `s 999(1) section 999 applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN IF NOT (`the copy of the articles is issued by the company after the order is made`)
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every copy of a company's articles issued by the company after the order is made" (a copy issued before the order is outside the period)
         ELSE IF `the effect of the order has been incorporated into the articles by amendment`
              THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the effect of the order has been incorporated into the articles by amendment"
              ELSE JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies where an order under this Part alters a company's constitution"

-- The company makes default in complying with section 999 if a copy that must accompany something did not.
-- Derived, not a provision (fork F2): subsection (4) speaks of "default in complying with this section".
-- src:13984 | (1) This section applies where an order under this Part alters a company's constitution.
-- src:13985 | (2) If the order amends—
-- src:13986 | (a) a company's articles, or
-- src:13987 | (b) any resolution or agreement to which Chapter 3 of Part 3 applies (resolution or agreement affecting a company's constitution),
-- src:13988 | the copy of the order delivered to the registrar by the company under section 998 must be accompanied by a copy of the company's articles, or the resolution or agreement in question, as amended.
-- src:13989 | (3) Every copy of a company's articles issued by the company after the order is made must be accompanied by a copy of the order, unless the effect of the order has been incorporated into the articles by amendment.
@ref s 999(4) Supplementary provisions where company's constitution altered (src:13984-13989)
GIVEN `s 999(2)(a) the copy of the order delivered to the registrar must be accompanied by a copy of the company's articles as amended` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the copy of the company's articles as amended accompanied the copy of the order delivered to the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 999(2)(b) the copy of the order delivered to the registrar must be accompanied by a copy of the resolution or agreement as amended` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the copy of the resolution or agreement as amended accompanied the copy of the order delivered to the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 999(3) the copy of the articles issued by the company must be accompanied by a copy of the order` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the copy of the order accompanied the copy of the articles issued by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 999(4) the company has made default in complying with section 999` MEANS
    IF     (`s 999(2)(a) the copy of the order delivered to the registrar must be accompanied by a copy of the company's articles as amended` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND NOT (`the copy of the company's articles as amended accompanied the copy of the order delivered to the registrar`))
       OR  (`s 999(2)(b) the copy of the order delivered to the registrar must be accompanied by a copy of the resolution or agreement as amended` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND NOT (`the copy of the resolution or agreement as amended accompanied the copy of the order delivered to the registrar`))
       OR  (`s 999(3) the copy of the articles issued by the company must be accompanied by a copy of the order` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND NOT (`the copy of the order accompanied the copy of the articles issued by the company`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "default in complying with this section" is not defined; a requirement that is not shown to apply cannot be shown to be breached

-- (4) If a company makes default in complying with section 999, an offence is committed by the company and by every
-- officer of the company who is in default.
-- src:13990 | (4) If a company makes default in complying with this section an offence is committed by—
-- src:13991 | (a) the company, and
-- src:13992 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 999(4) Supplementary provisions where company's constitution altered (src:13990-13992)
GIVEN `the company makes default in complying with section 999` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 999(4)(a) the company commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `the company makes default in complying with section 999`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company makes default in complying with this section an offence is committed by"

@ref s 999(4) Supplementary provisions where company's constitution altered (src:13990-13992)
GIVEN `the company makes default in complying with section 999` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 999(4)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the company makes default in complying with section 999`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company makes default in complying with this section an offence is committed by"
    ELSE IF `the person is an officer of the company` AND `s 1121 the officer is in default` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every officer of the company who is in default"; a person who is not an officer, or whom section 1121 does not find in default, is not named, and the seam may be open


-- (5) A person guilty of an offence under section 999 is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3
-- on the standard scale. There is no daily default fine.
-- src:13993 | (5) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 999(5) Supplementary provisions where company's constitution altered (src:13993)
`s 999(5) the penalty for a person guilty of an offence under section 999` MEANS
    Penalty OF `on summary conviction`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1), NOTHING, FALSE
